From ca7d38d232a3c90d5879162e604caad126960c5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:42:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/23] egl: clear the last error before each wglMakeCurrent()
 attempt

WglDisplay::makeCurrent() tells the error-less failure that it retries
from a real one by calling GetLastError() after wglMakeCurrent()
returns FALSE. Nothing clears the last error before the call, and
wglMakeCurrent() does not clear it either, so a failure that sets no
error code, which is the case the retry exists for, is judged by
whatever an earlier call on the same thread left behind: a stale error
ends the retries at once and reports a failure that might have been
retried.

Clear the last error before every attempt, so that what is read after
a failure comes from that wglMakeCurrent() call.

Test: on Windows 11 with an NVIDIA driver, a standalone program shows
      that a successful wglMakeCurrent() leaves a preset last error in
      place. In the emulator, a debugger made a render thread that had
      its own context current fail to bind a context that was current
      on another thread: with the last error cleared, the first
      attempt read 0 and was retried, the retry failed with 0xaa
      (ERROR_BUSY) and was reported, and teardownContext() bound the
      thread's context again.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:Claude-Opus-5.5
Change-Id: I019602fdadad1d6696dd6b39c0d1cb0603aa3622
---
 host/gl/glestranslator/egl/egl_os_api_wgl.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/host/gl/glestranslator/egl/egl_os_api_wgl.cpp b/host/gl/glestranslator/egl/egl_os_api_wgl.cpp
index fbb5502c..c8ca97a1 100644
--- a/host/gl/glestranslator/egl/egl_os_api_wgl.cpp
+++ b/host/gl/glestranslator/egl/egl_os_api_wgl.cpp
@@ -1159,7 +1159,14 @@ public:
             // context as current while none is, and its GL calls would go
             // nowhere. A failed release leaves no context current either, so
             // it still counts as done.
+            //
+            // wglMakeCurrent() does not necessarily set the last error when it
+            // fails, so clear it before every attempt: 0 must mean that this
+            // call failed without an error code, not that an earlier call on
+            // this thread happened to leave 0 behind (or a stale error that
+            // would make an error-less failure look like a real one).
             int count = 100;
+            SetLastError(0);
             while (!dispatch->wglMakeCurrent(hdcDraw, hdcContext)) {
                 const DWORD error = GetLastError();
                 if (!hdcContext) {
@@ -1170,6 +1177,7 @@ public:
                     return false;
                 }
                 Sleep(16);
+                SetLastError(0);
             }
             ret = true;
         } else if (!dispatch->wglMakeContextCurrent) {
